SUMMARY:LBC Bike to 30K Program: Ride #1 High Five
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Bicycle Club (LBC) Meetup\n**Grab your helmets\, bik
 es\, and sneakers — Lancaster Bicycle Club is gearing up for beginner an
 d transitional rides!** Local members of the LBC are thrilled to host this
  year’s **Bike to 30K Program**\, designed especially for new\, returnin
 g\, and curious cyclists.\n\n## **About the Program**\n\nBike to 30K is a 
 seven‑week series that gently builds your confidence\, fitness\, and mil
 eage. We start with a five‑mile ride and gradually work up to eighteen m
 iles by the end of the program. Our goal is simple: to introduce riders of
  all experience levels to the joy of cycling in a supportive\, community
 ‑focused environment.\n\nThis program is **FREE** with an LBC membership
 \, and membership is also free. The Bike to 30K program is open to everyon
 e in our community who wants to ride.\n\n## **Why We Ride**\n\nEver wonder
  why cyclists keep coming back? Because it’s fun. There’s nothing like
  coasting downhill and letting out a big “weeeeeee” all the way to the
  bottom. But we also know that if you’re new to cycling\, jumping straig
 ht into an 18‑mile ride can feel intimidating. That’s exactly why Bike
  to 30K exists.\n\nEach week\, you’ll increase your mileage at a comfort
 able pace. You’ll get to know the club\, meet fellow riders\, and gradua
 lly grow into a confident **Fun Rider** — the group known for enjoying s
 cenic\, social rides together.\n\n## **Our Commitment to You**\n\nLancaste
 r Bicycle Club is dedicated to supporting new riders and helping our commu
 nity reach their cycling goals. Bike to 30K is part of our initiative to e
 ncourage more people to get outside\, get active\, and discover how enjoya
 ble cycling can be.\n\nSpend seven weeks with us and watch yourself transf
 orm into a Fun Rider — one mile at a time.\n\nThe Bike to 30K program is
  voluntary\, welcoming\, and designed with beginners in mind. We can’t w
 ait to ride with you.\n\\*\\*\\*\nTo eliminate passing around a pen and pa
 per waiver\, we require an LBC Club membership and Meetup RSVP below to jo
 in this ride. Your RSVP also allows us to contact you after the ride if ne
 cessary. Please note ONLY club members who RSVP are covered by the club ex
 cess accident insurance policy. If you are a club member and do not RSVP\,
  you are not covered by the club excess accident insurance policy. Meetup 
 is our RSVP tool and being on Meetup does not mean you are a club member. 
 To join our wonderful club\, please [Join here](https://www.lancasterbikec
 lub.net/content.aspx?page_id=60&club_id=257148).\n\nPlease plan to arrive 
 10-15 minutes before the start time of the ride & make sure your bike is i
 n working condition. Helmets are mandatory\; please also plan to bring 1-2
  water bottles\, and basic repair kit (spare tube\, tire levers\, pump/CO2
  inflator). For everyone’s safety\, ear buds and music are not allowed.\
 n\n\\*\\*\\*\nRSVP is required and Your RSVP is your agreement to abide by
  the club's [Code of Conduct](https://lancbikeclub.clubexpress.com/content
 .aspx?page_id=22&club_id=257148&module_id=323984)\, the [Rules of the Road
 ](https://lancbikeclub.clubexpress.com/content.aspx?page_id=22&club_id=257
 148&module_id=325159) and Our [Ride Waiver](https://lancasterbikeclub.net/
 docs.ashx?id=454318).\n\\*\\*\\*\nWe've gone social! Join us on our Facebo
 ok Page: https://www.facebook.com/B230K\n• What to bring\nWater bottle\,
  bike\, helmet and sneakers\nCue Sheet to the Ride: [Ride #1 High Five](ht
 tps://routes.lancasterbikeclub.net/cue/mm-high-five-5f/)\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\
 \*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*
 \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\
 *\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n***The Bike to 30K is b
 rought to you by Lancaster Bicycle Club and Lancaster Trek Bikes.***
